      "message": "The ternary conditional operator (?:) has a pretty low precedence, lower than the \u003c\u003c operator.  So this code isn\u0027t going to do quite what we want.\n\nFor example, the code:\n\n  bool b \u003d true;\n  std::cout \u003c\u003c b ? \"yes\" : \"no\";\n\noutputs \"1\" (directly outputting the bool value), not \"yes\".\n\nI\u0027ve put up a follow-up fix: https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/hardware/interfaces/+/1982346",
